{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Versil","id":"148682928434577408","is_bot":0,"username":"versil"},"author_id":"148682928434577408","channel_id":"851856616469823528","content":"<@!343605682580488215> I have a more or less testing-ready implementation, with a few things to note:\n- it still needs three things to fill in the configuration: what time the new prices should get pulled from the spreadsheet, the url to the spreadsheet, and the name of the channel where transactions get announced\n\n- for now for testing purposes I can use the prices from the test sheet from the green rectangle, and direct stock announcements to ic-test-channel (it's getting deleted anyway), but I'll need the final values eventually\n\n- I don't think we discussed it, but I made an assumption based on intuition that you don't want people to sell stocks they don't have, so the logic as is now has the bot keep track of how many stocks of each company each player has and doesn't let them sell more than they have.\n\n- I'm still leaving in a possibility of manually prompting a price reload\n\n- will you be giving each company some short label like the three-letter ones irl? the work in progress I have right now would require players to specify the company by full name each time, the name being as it is listed in the spreadsheet","created_at":"2021-06-12T08:21:51.749000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"853187333452595220","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
